<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!-- The one line every App.axaml includes, and the one WiseMan's
         TestAppBuilder includes too - a headless render pass that misses the
         theme silently asserts over untemplated controls. See
         docs/LunaP.md §3.1. -->

    <FluentTheme />

    <!-- THE INDEX OF CONTROL STYLES. One file per control file in Controls/, so
         Theme/Controls/SplitPane.axaml sits opposite Controls/SplitPane.cs and
         there is never a question about which file a style belongs in. This was
         a single 508-line Controls.axaml until §29 split it.

         Every look here is the one the frontends already had; LunaPControlTests
         asserts these styles actually apply, because a selector that silently
         stops matching renders as an unstyled control rather than an error.
         See docs/LunaP.md §5.

         THE AutomationProperties.* ATTRIBUTES IN THESE FILES ARE LOAD-BEARING,
         not decoration. A template part that a keyboard can reach - a TextBox, a
         Button, a Dropdown - is announced by its accessible name and by nothing
         else, and every one of these was announced as "edit" or "Browse..." with
         no way to tell one from another. They are set in XAML rather than in
         code because a TemplateBinding is the whole of what each one needs, and
         because the name then lives beside the part it names. §24.2.

         A FILE THAT IS NOT LISTED BELOW IS A FILE THAT DOES NOTHING. Its styles
         are compiled and never reach the application, so its control has no
         template, renders as nothing, and raises no error - the §5.5 symptom,
         now reachable by forgetting a line here rather than by mistyping a
         selector.

         ALL SEVENTEEN OMISSIONS TURN THE SUITE RED, by four different guards
         and for four different reasons. It said SIXTEEN until §79.7, which is
         the count from before §48 added FormControls.axaml - the comment was
         not moved with the line. Corrected rather than quietly renumbered
         because this file's whole subject is that a missing entry is silent,
         and a note that miscounts the entries is the same class of thing it
         warns about. Dropping FormControls.axaml is caught by FormControlTests,
         which names the file and §48; verified by deleting the line and
         watching it turn red. Dropping a templated control's file is
         caught by TemplateReachTests, which requires a visual tree (§28.1);
         dropping TextControls.axaml is caught by LunaPControlTests, which reads
         the palette back off a SectionHeader, because a TextBlock has no
         template to miss; dropping MenuBar.axaml is caught by ShellTests, and
         only since §30 - it was the one file whose omission cost nothing, which
         is how the defect in §30 was found. Each was measured by deleting the
         line and running the suite: 11, 13 and 1 red respectively. §29.2 has
         the table.

         Order is the order the single file had, which is not load-bearing -
         every style below names a distinct control type, so none overrides
         another - but a diff against the old file is worth more than an
         alphabet.

         Three control files are deliberately absent. ActionControls, LunaList
         and Widgets (LunaSwitch, Dropdown, Tabs) carry StyleKeyOverride and
         borrow FluentTheme's templates wholesale, so they have no styles of
         their own to list - see §29.1. -->
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/TextControls.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/EmptyState.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/MeterRow.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/MeterList.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/RgbaImageView.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/FieldRow.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/PathPickerRow.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/Bars.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/FilterBar.axaml" />

    <!-- The shell: menu bar, toolbar, card, splitter, side panel. §26. -->
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/MenuBar.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/ToolBar.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/Card.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/SplitPane.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/LunaTable.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/SidePanel.axaml" />

    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/ConsolePane.axaml" />

    <!-- The form controls a stock Avalonia application is mostly made of. Almost
         all of that work is resource overrides in Theme/FluentBridge.axaml; this
         file is only the handful whose colours no resource key can reach. §48. -->
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Controls/FormControls.axaml" />

    <Styles.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
                <ResourceInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/Palette.axaml" />
                <!-- AFTER Palette.axaml, and that order is load-bearing: every
                     brush in the bridge points at a Luna colour key, so those
                     colours have to be in scope by the time it is merged. §48. -->
                <ResourceInclude Source="avares://EmuSen.LunaP/Theme/FluentBridge.axaml" />
            </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </Styles.Resources>

</Styles>
